= Biology =

== Scope ==
Biology studies living systems across scales: molecules, cells, organisms, populations, ecosystems, evolution, heredity, development, physiology, behavior, and the interactions that sustain or transform life.

== Includes ==
Cell and molecular biology, genetics/genomics, evolution, ecology, physiology, microbiology, developmental biology, organismal biology, biodiversity, biological processes and structures, and interdisciplinary work where living systems are central.

== Excludes / boundary ==
Medicine overlaps Biology but focuses on health, disease, diagnosis, treatment, and clinical practice. Chemistry and Physics may explain biological mechanisms without every underlying chemical or physical concept becoming primarily biological. Computational methods belong additionally in Computer science/Bioinformatics when computation is a defining part of the subject.

